%% OpenHub -- Beads ticket lifecycle as oh drives it (v5.1)
%% Beads (bd 1.3) statuses that oh uses: open, in_progress, blocked, closed.
%% There is no review status and no cancelled status in bd: REVIEW is an
%% in_progress ticket carrying the label ready-for-review (beads.BoardColumn),
%% and a cancelled ticket is closed with the label cancelled.
%% Other bd statuses (deferred, pinned, hooked) are not driven by oh and the
%% board shows them in TODO; custom statuses (validation, testing, qa,
%% pre-release) are shown in VALIDATION.

stateDiagram-v2
    state "in_progress + label ready-for-review (REVIEW)" as in_review

    [*] --> open

    open --> in_progress : bd update status in_progress
    open --> closed : cancelled, label cancelled then bd close

    in_progress --> blocked : blocked by a dependency
    blocked --> in_progress : unblocked

    in_progress --> in_review : agent adds the label
    in_review --> in_progress : review removes the label, back to development

    in_progress --> closed : bd close, or cancelled
    in_review --> closed : approved and merged

    closed --> [*]

    note right of in_review
        The status stays in_progress
        oh board and the TUI Board show the ticket in REVIEW
    end note

    note right of closed
        A closed ticket is not reopened by the agents
        The claim of the team-state moves to its terminal status
        at the end of the session
    end note
